data.content:
Three things break. Here's each one with the fix:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — no longer accepts expression trees

The parameter changed from `Expression<Func<...>>` to `Func<...>`. Your manual expression-tree code **won't compile**. Replace it with a simple lambda:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

This was the whole reason for the change — dynamic setters no longer need expression trees.

---

### 2. Complex type columns are now **uniquified** and nested paths are **fully qualified**

**Same-name properties** (e.g. `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`) previously shared one column silently. EF 10 appends a number (`Street`, `Street1`). If you have an existing database, add explicit column names to preserve the old mapping:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});
```

**Nested complex types** now use the full path. `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` was previously `BillingAddress_City`, now it's `Payment_BillingAddress_City`. To keep the old name:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

> **Tip:** After upgrading, run `dotnet ef migrations add UpgradeCheck`. If it generates column renames, add `HasColumnName` calls or apply the migration intentionally.

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

All methods (`CommandReaderExecuting`, `CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter. This string contains potentially-redacted SQL for safe logging. Update your signature:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (constants redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual executed SQL
    }
}
```

Update **every** method on the interface — they all gained this parameter.
